{{> header }}

<div class="row">
  <div class="col-md-12">
    <h1>Correction policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Decide how the employees of this company correct their recorded work sessions.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

{{> show_flash_messages }}

<div class="row">
  <div class="col-md-12">
    <div class="panel panel-default">
      <div class="panel-heading">How are corrections resolved?</div>
      <div class="panel-body">
        <form action="/settings/corrections/" method="POST">
          <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{@root.csrf_token}}">

          {{# each modes }}
            <div class="radio">
              <label>
                <input type="radio" name="mode" value="{{this.value}}" {{# if this.is_current}}checked="checked"{{/if}}>
                <strong>{{this.label}}</strong>
              </label>
            </div>
          {{/each}}

          <hr>

          <p class="text-muted">
            With <strong>approval required</strong> (the default for a company that has never
            configured anything) a correction is sent to the supervisor of the employee and only
            changes the record once it is approved.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            With <strong>self-service</strong> the correction is applied as soon as the employee
            sends it. The original clock-in, clock-out and breaks are preserved either way, and every
            change is audited.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            Changing this setting does not approve pending requests, does not revert corrections that
            were already applied and does not modify the history: each request keeps the policy that
            applied when it was submitted.
          </p>

          <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Save policy</button>
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{{> footer }}
